  "sourceFindings": [
    "Prayer 469–484 adds sixteen complete selected numbered reports, forty-five English segments and nine complete digital chapters (88–96). All selected Arabic paragraphs and all prior 468 entry objects remain unchanged. The source-only heading at chapter 89 is separately browseable and never becomes a daily-session entry.",
    "Historical print PDF pages 132–137 and modern print PDF pages 128–132 were visually inspected. Modern labels 483–506 were matched individually. The nine accounts numbered 484–492 in the modern print remain the single selected entry 470, with repeated attributions and thirteen honorifics retained.",
    "The Khan-family EPUB reference 1.8.471 contains an omission notice rather than a translation of selected 470. The importer now classifies that exact body without changing its bytes. Admission requires its explicit omitted-translation status, exact pinned record and notice; removing the status or using the notice as a translated part fails validation. Source details accurately state that only one complete English comparison was available.",
    "470 retains the full geographical account, both tree terms, measures without metric conversion, uncertainties, repeated mosque wording and changes of grammatical person. Ibn Hajar’s lexical discussion and Dorar’s tree-antecedent explanation were consulted separately. The selected until differs from the historical when; rocks follows one vocalization of salimat. These provisional choices remain pending independent lexical and geographical review.",
    "Bewley 469–470 are on bukhari5; 471–484 are on bukhari6. Per-report source references now preserve that page change without replacing earlier citations. The Khan-family references for 471–483 are in Book 9; the Prayer configuration explicitly permits Books 8 and 9, with exact evidence required across the edition boundary.",
    "471 retains nearing puberty and without facing a wall. 473 retains passing in front of him, while 477 retains beyond it and does not acquire an absent two-rakah count. 474 does not import a head/prostration gloss. 475–476 preserve unexpanded names, 478 all three implement alternatives, and 479 the selected order of events. 480 retains the singular written Quran copy and selected Prophet wording.",
    "469, 472, 481, 483 and 484 retain visible closing transmission notes. 481 preserves Shu‘bah / ‘Amr / Anas. 483 preserves one right-hand pillar in the first account and two in the separately attributed closing transmission, without harmonization.",
    "Selected 484 is absent between adjacent pinned English records 1.9.484 and 1.9.485, which match selected 483 and 485. Both Arabic prints and Bewley contain it. The checked absence and the prints’ untitled chapter division are disclosed; the selected digital chapter grouping remains.",
    "One original Arabic chapter introduction at chapter 95 remains separately browseable and saved offline, with English pending. Its selected and modern Umar attribution differs from the historical Ibn Umar and is recorded. The introduction and standalone heading stay outside numbered sessions and narration. All seven other active book files, existing recordings and artwork remain unchanged."
  ],
